<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Deliberately empty, and that is the decision this file records.

	     keychain-access-groups is ABSENT. It was here from 2026-09-12 so the listener could read
	     source credentials and probe secrets from a shared access group, and it stopped the
	     listener from ever running: the key is profile-backed, AMFI honours it only when an
	     embedded provisioning profile authorizes it, and this is a bare executable in
	     Contents/Helpers, which cannot embed one. launchd's every spawn ended with
	     OS_REASON_CODESIGNING ("Code has restricted entitlements, but the validation of its code
	     signature failed") while the signature itself verified and ServiceManagement still
	     reported the job enabled.

	     Trigger secrets are login-Keychain items whose access list names the app and this helper
	     by designated requirement instead (TriggerDaemonContract.swift), which needs no
	     entitlement on either side. scripts/check_bundle_entitlements.py refuses any
	     profile-backed key on a bundled helper, so this cannot come back unnoticed.

	     com.apple.security.app-sandbox is ABSENT for the same reason as threading-ptyd's: a probe
	     is the person's own unsandboxed program, run as them. Hardened runtime is on with no
	     exceptions. -->
</dict>
</plist>
